==Strategy==
==='''Chapters 1 & 2'''===
Start by getting 2 levels into your Worker Cat so that you can save enough money from the mass of Doge Darks to spawn your heavies and zombie killers. Cadaver Bear is a tough enemy, no way around that. He hits faster and harder than Teacher Bear and his 360 range area attacks mean you shouldn't use anything below 400 honestly as he will just walk up to them easily. He's kind of a more friendly Assassin Bear so do not underestimate it.

The Doge Darks provide all the cash flow you need to fight Ursamajor but once Cadaver Bear spawns the Doge flow starts to slow down and you will have to rely on the fact that you spawned the right units with the cash you had. Ursamajor should fall relatively quickly and then you're just left with the Cadaver Bear who wants to sneak past your front line and whack your base. Still, if you have Giraffe Cats or fast rushers like A. Bahamut, you can just put the hurt on Cadaver Bear until he burrows and take out the base.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
This is the exact same stage as Chapter 3, possibly with more Doge Darks but it was hardly noticeable. Only 2 Ursamajors spawn, one at 30 seconds and the other 90 seconds into the stage. Only 2 Cadaver Bears spawn. The units are buffed through the roof but the strategy remains the same. Bring anti-Dark cats to deal with the Doge Darks as they can give good cash at the start before you have to deal with the bears.

With the support of other units, it is possible to time A. Bahamut to kill the first Ursamajor before cadaver bear #1 finishes its burrow. If enough meatshields slip through alongside A. Bahamut, they can hold off the Doge Darks while Bahamut kills the base, ensuring a cheesy victory. Make sure you can hold off the unburrowed cadaver bear; use whatever cat cannon you have to keep it away from your base and use meat shields ([[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Sifu Cat]] is a great option) to ensure victory.

